# What never goes into the build context. This file is why `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile is safe: without it, the secrets and the patient data below would
# be baked into an image layer, where deleting them later does not remove them.

# Reinstalled from package-lock.json inside the build stage. Copying a
# Windows-built node_modules into a Linux image would also ship the wrong
# native bcrypt binary.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# History is not needed to run the app, and it is the bulk of the context.
.git
.gitignore

# Secrets. In a container these arrive as real environment variables from the
# platform or from docker-compose - never from a file in the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Uploaded ID images. Deleted inside the request that reads them, so this is
# normally empty; excluded so that a stray file can never be shipped.
uploads

*.log
server_pid.txt

# Dev-only artifacts.
graphify-out
.claude
.agents
*.tmp.js
__pycache__

# A scratchpad backup whose destination path was flattened into its filename.
# It contains deleted customers' usernames, emails and full names.
UserswendelleAppDataLocalTemp*

# No point invalidating a layer over the build definition itself.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
DOCKER.md
